  "goodToKnow": "Demokratisch means democratic: demokratische Wahlen (democratic elections). Ironically, East Germany called itself the Deutsche Demokratische Republik (DDR) although it was a one-party state, which led to the joke that any country with 'democratic' in its name isn't one. Demokratisch abstimmen means to decide by vote. The opposite is undemokratisch, and the root is die Demokratie."
